{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringConeGauge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringConeGauge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BringCone"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.isUnit_two_of_triadGauge_i_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.isUnit_two_of_triadGauge_i_j","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L260-L291","doc":"**If `Γ_i` and `Γ_j` are triad-gauge-equivalent, then `2` is a unit.** So over a\nring in which `2` is not invertible (e.g. `ℤ`), the choice of `u` is NOT a gauge\nchoice: `Γ_i` and `Γ_j` are inequivalent under the commutant of the Reeb triad. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.exists_triad_equiv_conj_chiralGammaU_ordered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.exists_triad_equiv_conj_chiralGammaU_ordered","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L215-L254","doc":"**Over a linearly ordered field (e.g. `ℝ`), any two pure units give\ngauge-equivalent gradings.** No hypothesis beyond `u`, `v` being points of `S²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigen_eq_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigen_eq_U","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L197-L200","doc":"`reebM_j_flips_eigen` (BringCone) is the `u = i` case of `reebM_j_flips_eigenU`: `Γ_i = Γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_preserves_eigenU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_preserves_eigenU","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L190-L195","doc":"`M_i` preserves each chirality, for every `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_k_flips_eigenU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_k_flips_eigenU","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L184-L188","doc":"`M_k` also exchanges the two chiralities, for every `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigenU'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigenU'","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L179-L182","doc":"`M_j` sends a `Γ_u = +1` vector to a `Γ_u = −1` vector, for every `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigenU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigenU","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L173-L177","doc":"`M_j` sends a `Γ_u = −1` vector to a `Γ_u = +1` vector, for every `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.symm","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L156-L162","doc":"The inverse of a triad gauge transformation is one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.eigen_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.eigen_neg","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L150-L154","doc":"`e` carries a `Γ_u = −1` vector to a `Γ_v = −1` vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.eigen_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.eigen_iff","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L142-L148","doc":"**Eigenvectors are carried to eigenvectors with the same eigenvalue.** This is\nthe covariant content of `chiralGamma_apply`: the `Γ_v`-eigenspaces are the\n`e`-images of the `Γ_u`-eigenspaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.exists_triad_equiv_conj_chiralGammaU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.exists_triad_equiv_conj_chiralGammaU","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L117-L134","doc":"**The choice of `u` is a gauge choice.** For pure units `u`, `v`, a triad gauge\ntransformation `Γ_u → Γ_v` exists, provided either `2·(1 + u·v)` is a unit (then\n`L_{1−vu}` works), or `v = −u` and some pure `w ⊥ u` has invertible norm (then\n`L_w` works). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.mul_eq_neg_mul_of_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.mul_eq_neg_mul_of_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L108-L113","doc":"For pure `u`, `w` with `u ⊥ w`: `w·u = (−u)·w`, i.e. they anticommute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.ofIntertwiner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.ofIntertwiner","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L82-L106","doc":"**A quaternion `q` with `q·u = v·q` and invertible norm is a triad gauge\ntransformation `Γ_u → Γ_v`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMulEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMulEquiv","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L72-L80","doc":"Left multiplication by an invertible quaternion, as a linear equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.conj","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.comm_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.comm_k","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.comm_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.comm_j","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.comm_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.comm_i","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.e","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The automorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.TriadGauge","kind":"structure","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L62-L70","doc":"A **triad gauge transformation** from `Γ_u` to `Γ_v`: an `R`-linear automorphism\nof the cone that commutes with each Reeb operator and intertwines the two gradings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.imDot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.imDot","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeGauge.lean#L59-L60","doc":"Euclidean dot product of the imaginary parts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}